[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Buff" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://cqrqkdgcf8mti" path="res://engine/character/buff/buff.gd" id="1_buff"]
[ext_resource type="Texture2D" path="res://unpacked/Reag-TheSixthVoice/res/assets/frames/icons/cp_quietus_machines.svg" id="2_icon"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_buff")
; THE MYCONID'S OWN "FUNGAL NETWORK IS RUNNING" CHIP, and a dummy: it announces the zone and does
; nothing else. The author asked for it after playtesting - "we should probably put a dummy chip on
; the Myconid that has activated Fungal Network (shares icon with the core power) so that you can
; tell its running at a glance" - because the cloud draws nothing on the map and the Myconid, alone
; of everyone standing in it, wore nothing to say the protocol had been pressed. Its allies get two
; chips, its enemies get one and two status icons, and the unit the whole thing hangs off got none.
;
; EFFECT-LESS IS ENOUGH TO BE DRAWN, WHICH IS THE FACT THIS FILE RESTS ON. mech_info.gd:34 puts
; every buff without hide_from_player into the unit's chip row and tooltip_organ_unit.gd:130 does the
; same for the inspector; neither consults `to`, applies_statuses, triggers_on or anything else about
; the Buff. Vanilla says so outright twenty lines further down that same file:
; tooltip_organ_unit.gd:149, skipping an actionless trait in the loadout list, reads "if an empty
; trait wants to make itself known, it'll do so via a visible buff". buff_gather_round.tres - the
; Subutai's core-power chip - is this mod's own precedent for the shape: a plain Buff whose entire
; content is an icon.
;
; `to` IS SPELLED OUT even though &"none" is the export's default (buff.gd:123), because it is the
; one thing here worth being unable to miss. The card gives the Myconid ITSELF nothing, so a channel
; on this chip would be a rules change nobody asked for - and a silent one, since no other test in
; test_fungal_network.gd would notice. test_the_chip_carries_no_mechanical_effect pins it, together
; with the empty applies_statuses and triggers_on.
to = &"none"
icon = ExtResource("2_icon")
; DELIBERATELY VISIBLE: hide_from_player stays at its false default (buff.gd:127), because being
; seen is the whole job. test_content_integrity.gd's VISIBLE_BUFFS lists it, and its size assertion
; is what stops the pair drifting apart.
;
; SP3'S ICON PASS: THIS CHIP SHARES THE CORE POWER'S ICON, AND THE ENGINE ALREADY DOES THAT FOR
; FREE. BuffCore.get_icon falls back to the OWNER GEAR'S KIT ICON when the Buff itself declares none
; - `if base.icon: return base.icon` then `owner_gear.kit.icon_and_flavor().icon`
; (buff_core.gd:81-86) - and this chip's owner gear IS cp_quietus_machines, because
; PassiveAura.apply_aura_buffs_to_unit stamps the aura gear as the source (passive_aura.gd:82 hands
; aura_gear to UnitCondition.apply_buffs, which writes it onto the BuffCore at unit_condition.gd:706
; and :709) and get_owner_gear resolves it back off from_gear (buff_core.gd:113-116). So the
; author's instruction is the engine's own default behaviour with no property set at all, and it is
; already true today.
;
; SP3 MUST STILL SET AN EXPLICIT icon, and should know it is satisfying a GUARD rather than creating
; the behaviour: test_content_integrity.gd:398 reads `buff.icon` RAW - the field, not
; Buff.get_icon() - so the fallback above is invisible to it and a null field fails the row however
; the chip actually draws. Point it at whatever cp_quietus_machines.tres ends up wearing (the KIT's
; icon is what the fallback resolves to, not action_fungal_network.tres's), and do NOT invent a new
; icon for it.
;
; `until` stays at its MANUAL default for the reason every other buff in this folder gives: the AURA
; owns the lifetime. passive_fungal_network_self.tres applies and clears it, and
; PassiveAura.update_unit does both off the Kit's single is_aura_active flag (passive_aura.gd:37,
; :55-59). Any `until` short of MANUAL would let the chip expire on a clock of its own while the zone
; was still up - which is the same lie this chip exists to prevent, told the other way round.
